1
00:00:05,980 --> 00:00:08,940
YAMU! YAMU! YAMU! YAMU!

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,520
Your moves!

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:39,320
It's time to duel!

4
00:01:01,520 --> 00:01:03,480
We're almost there, Serenity.

5
00:01:03,860 --> 00:01:04,820
Thanks, Taya.

6
00:01:05,080 --> 00:01:07,620
I have to see this place before I go home.

7
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:11,817
I mean, this is the town where the
entire Battle City tournament began.

8
00:01:11,900 --> 00:01:14,417
You gotta make sure we
hit every single spot.

9
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,441
You're getting the complete tour.

10
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:20,000
Now for stop number
one, the Domino Museum.

11
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:22,150
Hello.

12
00:01:22,233 --> 00:01:23,063
Stick together, kids.

13
00:01:23,146 --> 00:01:25,198
What time is there a gift shop here?

14
00:01:25,660 --> 00:01:27,280
Notice anything familiar?

15
00:01:28,220 --> 00:01:29,180
I do.

16
00:01:29,520 --> 00:01:30,755
That looks like Yugi.

17
00:01:31,060 --> 00:01:34,037
Is this the stone tablet
everyone was talking about?

18
00:01:34,120 --> 00:01:34,950
Yup.

19
00:01:35,033 --> 00:01:36,346
This is where it all started.

20
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:39,460
My Pharaoh, I've been expecting you.

21
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:43,120
Who are you?

22
00:01:43,400 --> 00:01:45,340
I am Ishizu.

23
00:01:45,540 --> 00:01:49,775
And I have uncovered many mysteries
about you and these ancient carvings

24
00:01:49,960 --> 00:01:52,520
using the magic of my Millennium necklace.

25
00:01:53,800 --> 00:01:55,237
Another Millennium item.

26
00:01:55,320 --> 00:02:00,160
Like your millennium puzzle, this
necklace affords me certain powers.

27
00:02:00,560 --> 00:02:04,097
With it, I have gazed
5,000 years into the past,

28
00:02:04,180 --> 00:02:08,500
to a time when evil sorcerers
threatened to destroy the entire world.

29
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:10,930
However,

30
00:02:11,013 --> 00:02:15,840
there was one king who possessed a magic
powerful enough to stop this evil threat.

31
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:17,500
And who was this king?

32
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:20,857
The pharaoh who saved
the world was you, Yami.

33
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:25,440
And now the time has come for
you to rescue mankind once again.

34
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:27,940
To rescue mankind from what?

35
00:02:28,140 --> 00:02:31,757
How do you know the world is in
danger of being destroyed again?

36
00:02:31,840 --> 00:02:35,700
My Millennium Necklace also
shows me visions of the future.

37
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:37,400
Oh, my pharaoh.

38
00:02:39,020 --> 00:02:41,800
The events of the past
will occur once again.

39
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:45,340
And that same great evil
will return to threaten us.

40
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:49,260
So that's why Yugi joined
the Battle City Tournament.

41
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:50,250
That's right.

42
00:02:50,333 --> 00:02:53,880
And when Joey found out, he joined
to help Yugi save the world.

43
00:02:56,660 --> 00:02:59,957
This is where Joey fought his
first duel of the tournament,

44
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,820
against that lame-o Esperoba.

45
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:03,160
You want a duel?

46
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:06,880
Take my advice and stay
away from this freak.

47
00:03:07,180 --> 00:03:08,660
He's Esperoba.

48
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,820
He duels using ESP.

49
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,440
You mean he's psycho?

50
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:13,920
No, psychic.

51
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:16,257
He'll mind-read the cards in your hand.

52
00:03:16,340 --> 00:03:19,105
He'll know what move
you'll make before you do.

53
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,190
Let's duel!

54
00:03:25,540 --> 00:03:26,370
That's right!

55
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:28,815
I remember everything about this duel.

56
00:03:29,020 --> 00:03:31,297
I was in the hospital
after my eye operation

57
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:33,909
and Tristan was giving
me the play-by-play.

58
00:03:35,160 --> 00:03:37,420
My big brothers never let me down.

59
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:41,080
Now it's my turn to do
whatever I can to help out.

60
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:46,462
I may not be next to him, but can you help
me be with him in spirit, pretty please?

61
00:03:47,140 --> 00:03:48,400
You bet I can.

62
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:52,277
Now let's get back to the duel and cheer
that brother of yours till he wins.

63
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,190
Great.

64
00:03:55,180 --> 00:03:56,380
It's showtime!

65
00:03:57,520 --> 00:04:01,461
I'll sacrifice your swords in the
Blanchthor and I'll summon Jinzo!

66
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:05,940
The end is near, Wheeler.

67
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:25,900
You're mine, Wheeler!

68
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:30,480
Now, Jinso, attack his thousand
dragon with cyber energy shot!

69
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:39,480
Now that my dragon's gone,
how long can I hold on?

70
00:04:42,700 --> 00:04:43,720
Wait a sec.

71
00:04:44,800 --> 00:04:48,437
This is where I saw Joey dueling
for the first time, isn't it?

72
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,873
Yeah, this is the spot.

73
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:54,580
To tell you the truth, Serenity, it
was one of the worst days of my life.

74
00:04:56,580 --> 00:04:57,880
Oh, no! Taya!

75
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:02,380
This may come as an unpleasant
surprise, but like your friend Joey,

76
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,740
Taya too is under my control.

77
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:08,090
Surprised?

78
00:05:08,173 --> 00:05:09,920
Merrick, leave her alone now!

79
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:11,869
She's done nothing to you!

80
00:05:12,800 --> 00:05:17,217
Looks like I've turned your closest
friends into your greatest enemies!

81
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,920
You're at my mercy.

82
00:05:19,640 --> 00:05:20,470
Teya!

83
00:05:22,440 --> 00:05:25,320
I've attacked your life
points yet again, Yugi.

84
00:05:26,860 --> 00:05:27,860
You're finished.

85
00:05:28,140 --> 00:05:30,140
As soon as I wipe out the rest,

86
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:33,888
that anchor will drop, taking
you with it right into the sea.

87
00:05:34,040 --> 00:05:38,037
Merrick, I can assure you that
you'll never get away with your plan.

88
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:43,460
Ignore that fool, my servant, and use your
Meteor of Destruction to finish him off.

89
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,497
As soon as you play that card,

90
00:05:45,580 --> 00:05:50,300
Little Yu-Gi will receive 1,000 points
worth of damage, destroying him.

91
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:53,107
And his most prized
possessions will be mine.

92
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:56,937
Now do as I command and deliver
the final strike against him.

93
00:05:57,020 --> 00:05:58,080
This is it, Joey.

94
00:05:58,320 --> 00:06:00,496
You have to remember who you are now.

95
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:02,000
Now destroy him.

96
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:03,960
Destroy Yu-Gi.

97
00:06:04,080 --> 00:06:05,437
Get out of my head.

98
00:06:05,520 --> 00:06:08,160
Your feeble brain is no match for me.

99
00:06:08,900 --> 00:06:11,780
So play Meteor of Destruction now.

100
00:06:12,040 --> 00:06:14,217
You belong to me. Understand?

101
00:06:14,300 --> 00:06:17,080
And I command you to vanquish Yugi!

102
00:06:17,380 --> 00:06:18,260
I can't!

103
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,600
He's my best friend!

104
00:06:19,900 --> 00:06:21,480
I won't destroy Yugi!

105
00:06:23,400 --> 00:06:26,097
It's a good thing your brother
has such a strong head,

106
00:06:26,180 --> 00:06:28,697
or he never would have
broken Marek's mind control.

107
00:06:28,780 --> 00:06:31,097
But it's not like I have to tell you that.

108
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:33,237
You were there to see it all yourself.

109
00:06:33,320 --> 00:06:34,820
Mm-hmm. I know.

110
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:39,982
It was Joey's bravery that gave me the
confidence I needed to take my bandages off.

111
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:43,512
Of course, I never could have
imagined what happened next.

112
00:06:57,320 --> 00:07:02,000
I can see Hang in there, Uke

113
00:07:02,620 --> 00:07:04,973
You'll be out of those chains in no time

114
00:07:10,660 --> 00:07:11,720
It's Joey

115
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:14,380
Almost there.

116
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:16,300
Got to beat the clock.

117
00:07:24,100 --> 00:07:27,100
That anchor's going to
drag both of them down.

118
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:29,090
Joey!

119
00:07:29,960 --> 00:07:30,790
Tristan!

120
00:07:36,880 --> 00:07:38,780
Yugi, I'll save you.

121
00:07:43,200 --> 00:07:45,259
I told you I wouldn't let you down.

122
00:07:48,980 --> 00:07:49,810
Serenity!

123
00:07:50,140 --> 00:07:51,500
She's got the key.

124
00:07:54,980 --> 00:07:55,810
Serenity?

125
00:08:00,780 --> 00:08:02,020
She did it!

126
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:06,660
I thought the insanity
was over after that.

127
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:08,340
Boy, was I wrong.

128
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:14,040
It was off to the Battle
City Finals for more madness.

129
00:08:14,460 --> 00:08:15,780
All right, listen up!

130
00:08:16,040 --> 00:08:20,452
It's time to board Kaiba Craft III for
the start of the Battle City Finals!

131
00:08:23,940 --> 00:08:24,770
Yugi,

132
00:08:24,853 --> 00:08:28,837
I'm aware that you haven't played your
Egyptian God card since you won it,

133
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,537
but it's time for that to
end right here and now.

134
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:34,561
And then when the Battle
City Finals are all over,

135
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:40,540
I'll be the world's greatest duelist and
the owner of all three Egyptian God Cards,

136
00:08:40,720 --> 00:08:42,520
making my deck unbeatable.

137
00:08:44,600 --> 00:08:48,000
Prepare to experience
a power like no other!

138
00:08:54,420 --> 00:08:59,160
I summon the almighty
Swiper the Sky Dragon!

139
00:09:17,460 --> 00:09:20,297
and now i will summon my egyptian god

140
00:09:20,380 --> 00:09:25,300
card show yourself obelisk the tormentor

141
00:09:37,640 --> 00:09:39,200
Ha ha ha ha ha!

142
00:09:42,260 --> 00:09:47,520
Unlock your powers from deep
within, so that together we may win!

143
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:50,980
Appear in this shadow
game as I call your name!

144
00:09:51,300 --> 00:09:53,440
Win the Dragon of Wrath!

145
00:09:56,500 --> 00:09:59,660
It's time now to end this duel!

146
00:10:04,940 --> 00:10:06,557
Boy, it's getting kinda chilly.

147
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,260
Hmm, we should get going.

148
00:10:08,800 --> 00:10:11,140
Yeah, there's still plenty left to see.

149
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:22,940
Next, I'll sacrifice Rocket Warrior in
order to summon my Jinzo to the field.

150
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:30,540
Wow, check out all these kids dueling.

151
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:33,897
I bet they all want to grow
up to be champion duelists.

152
00:10:33,980 --> 00:10:37,717
And thanks to Kaiba Corp, they can
get all the practice that they need.

153
00:10:37,800 --> 00:10:40,697
Because now these virtual
duels can happen anywhere.

154
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:43,260
Next, I'll place two cards face down.

155
00:10:43,440 --> 00:10:45,780
It's so cute to see kids dueling.

156
00:10:46,020 --> 00:10:46,900
Not quite.

157
00:10:49,620 --> 00:10:50,740
Uh, sorry.

158
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:55,760
You just reminded me of that kid
Noah, and he was anything but cute.

159
00:10:56,100 --> 00:10:59,688
Look, Noah, you overpowered Kai
by using deceit and betrayal.

160
00:10:59,900 --> 00:11:03,557
Then you used your virtual technology
to turn him and Mokuba into stone.

161
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:07,900
If you think that makes you a superior
duelist, you're sadly mistaken.

162
00:11:08,420 --> 00:11:10,420
Yugi, we're all here for you.

163
00:11:10,580 --> 00:11:13,397
Since you're all so confident
that Yugi's going to win,

164
00:11:13,480 --> 00:11:16,080
I've decided to put
your fate in his hands.

165
00:11:16,440 --> 00:11:19,264
So with every turn that
Yugi fails to defeat me,

166
00:11:19,420 --> 00:11:21,714
another of you will be turned to stone.

167
00:11:21,820 --> 00:11:25,408
You'll be frozen in time with
a look of despair on your face.

168
00:11:25,980 --> 00:11:28,297
Because Yugi failed to save you.

169
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:30,220
And in the end, Yu-Gi,

170
00:11:30,420 --> 00:11:32,457
you'll be left in the
middle of a circle of

171
00:11:32,540 --> 00:11:35,500
motionless statues that
were once your friends.

172
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,160
Say goodbye!

173
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:42,600
No, Chewie!

174
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:45,340
I will save my friends.

175
00:11:45,720 --> 00:11:46,677
Just watch me.

176
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:49,500
You insist on humiliating
yourself, don't you?

177
00:11:49,680 --> 00:11:52,160
I won't stop until you're defeated, Noah.

178
00:11:52,460 --> 00:11:54,440
I play Monster Reborn!

179
00:11:54,780 --> 00:11:57,497
It can revive any monster
you sent to the graveyard,

180
00:11:57,580 --> 00:12:00,880
including Kaiba's Blue-Eyes White Dragon.

181
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,800
It can't be.

182
00:12:03,040 --> 00:12:05,960
Now I activate this card, Polymerization.

183
00:12:06,460 --> 00:12:09,417
This allows me to fuse
my Blue-Eyes on the field

184
00:12:09,500 --> 00:12:12,206
with the two other
Blue-Eyes cards in my hand.

185
00:12:15,420 --> 00:12:19,500
Now, behold the power of my
Blue-Eyes Ultimate Dragon.

186
00:12:22,020 --> 00:12:24,957
Next, I'll activate my
Quick Attack Magic card.

187
00:12:25,040 --> 00:12:28,160
This lets my dragon attack right now!

188
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:31,040
Hino Kadosuchi is finished!

189
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,180
It's not over yet!

190
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:37,760
Noah, you're wrong!

191
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:42,360
Thanks to the next magic
card in my hand, D-Fusion!

192
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:46,880
And separates my beast back
into three separate dragons,

193
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:49,180
each with 3,000 attack points!

194
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,900
No, wait!

195
00:12:51,100 --> 00:12:52,617
There must be something I can do!

196
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:56,520
You've been exposed as the
frightened child you truly are.

197
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,580
Blue-Eyes White Dragons, attack!

198
00:13:00,540 --> 00:13:01,620
Wipe him out!

199
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:08,860
This madness is finally over, Noah!

200
00:13:10,360 --> 00:13:12,920
Well, it wasn't his fault.

201
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:15,081
Noah was just lonely, that's all.

202
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:16,680
He had no friends.

203
00:13:17,160 --> 00:13:21,057
Yeah, he was just bitter because he
had no one to play with for so long.

204
00:13:21,140 --> 00:13:24,060
Time to bring out my Summoned Skull!

205
00:13:27,860 --> 00:13:31,560
But in the end, Noah
realized he was wrong. Yeah.

206
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:34,240
I'm glad I got to know my brother.

207
00:13:34,700 --> 00:13:37,137
So, does this mean you're not coming back?

208
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:40,197
I'm afraid there's something
I still have to do, Mokuba.

209
00:13:40,280 --> 00:13:43,380
I'm sorry, but I can't let you hurt them.

210
00:13:43,580 --> 00:13:45,800
So I'm keeping you trapped in here.

211
00:13:46,240 --> 00:13:47,360
Sound familiar?

212
00:13:48,180 --> 00:13:49,217
What are you doing?

213
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:53,240
I command you to release
me immediately, Noah!

214
00:13:55,040 --> 00:13:59,220
I'm going to free your mind and make
sure you never harm anyone again.

215
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:04,460
Warning, virtual meltdown.

216
00:14:05,200 --> 00:14:06,240
No, let me go!

217
00:14:06,380 --> 00:14:07,733
You can't keep me here!

218
00:14:11,480 --> 00:14:15,060
At least Noah got to feel what
it's like to have friends.

219
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,540
Good point.

220
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:21,220
Hey, nice duel!

221
00:14:21,500 --> 00:14:23,697
Yeah, nice because I kicked your butt!

222
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:25,560
That's because I let you win!

223
00:14:26,620 --> 00:14:28,080
Now let's play again!

224
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:30,020
These kids are kinda cute.

225
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:32,420
But they're only dueling for fun.

226
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:36,780
When Yugi dueled in Battle
City, a lot more was at stake.

227
00:14:37,440 --> 00:14:38,660
Yugi, wait up!

228
00:14:39,280 --> 00:14:42,692
So you're actually gonna go
ahead with this duel up there?

229
00:14:42,780 --> 00:14:47,074
Did you forget how many people have
gotten hurt in the tournament so far?

230
00:14:47,580 --> 00:14:49,345
Please, Yugi, enough's enough.

231
00:14:49,660 --> 00:14:52,248
I can't stand the thought
of losing you two.

232
00:14:52,420 --> 00:14:53,660
Just end it.

233
00:14:53,860 --> 00:14:55,817
It's not worth all this suffering.

234
00:14:55,900 --> 00:14:58,780
This tournament's been
nothing but bad news.

235
00:14:59,420 --> 00:15:00,250
I know.

236
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:05,280
But if I walk away now, that means
everyone suffered for nothing.

237
00:15:07,680 --> 00:15:11,337
Taya, remember what we learned
on our trip to the Domino Museum?

238
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:12,640
About my destiny?

239
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:16,250
Yes.

240
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:20,557
We found out that you were
a pharaoh in ancient Egypt,

241
00:15:20,640 --> 00:15:22,757
and that now you need
to save the world again

242
00:15:22,840 --> 00:15:26,580
from some evil thingy like
you did 5,000 years ago.

243
00:15:28,160 --> 00:15:28,990
Taya!

244
00:15:29,073 --> 00:15:32,597
Do you now understand why backing out
of the tournament is not an option?

245
00:15:32,680 --> 00:15:33,510
Yeah, but...

246
00:15:33,593 --> 00:15:34,423
No buts, Taya!

247
00:15:34,506 --> 00:15:37,517
The reason I joined the Battle
City Tournament was to fulfill

248
00:15:37,600 --> 00:15:41,700
Ashizu's prophecy and stop this
great evil from endangering mankind.

249
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:47,980
And when Joey found out, he vowed to
help me, no matter how tough the fight.

250
00:15:48,620 --> 00:15:50,640
And that's why I must press on.

251
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:53,722
Otherwise, not only would
I be giving up on Joey,

252
00:15:53,820 --> 00:15:55,996
I'd be giving up on the entire world.

253
00:15:56,140 --> 00:15:57,997
There's too much at stake to lose.

254
00:15:58,080 --> 00:15:59,680
We're right here. Good.

255
00:16:02,140 --> 00:16:04,140
I know you can win this, Yugi.

256
00:16:05,100 --> 00:16:06,977
The last duel's about to begin.

257
00:16:07,060 --> 00:16:11,980
Marek Ishtar will face Yugimoto, and the
winner will receive the Battle City Crown.

258
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:14,740
Let the fun begin now!

259
00:16:15,740 --> 00:16:16,760
Oh, no.

260
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,660
It's another Shadow Game.

261
00:16:18,900 --> 00:16:23,637
You've witnessed several of my Shadow Games
before, but this one will be different.

262
00:16:23,720 --> 00:16:27,420
I've thrown in a few
twists, especially for you.

263
00:16:29,740 --> 00:16:31,900
Meet my next victim.

264
00:16:35,640 --> 00:16:36,760
Oh, no!

265
00:16:37,060 --> 00:16:40,820
Lose the duel and Yugi
goes to the Shadow Realm!

266
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:44,336
Merrick, this is about you
and me, so leave him alone!

267
00:16:44,580 --> 00:16:45,600
That's not true!

268
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,000
You're forgetting my weaker hat!

269
00:16:49,240 --> 00:16:52,100
He's involved in this conflict as well!

270
00:16:52,540 --> 00:16:55,500
So if I lose, the shadows will take him!

271
00:16:55,820 --> 00:16:57,060
No, you can't!

272
00:16:57,220 --> 00:16:58,580
I just did!

273
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:03,160
The Shadow Realm will claim an
innocent soul no matter who wins!

274
00:17:09,620 --> 00:17:12,537
Showing serenity around
town brought back so many

275
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:15,797
memories about my friends in
the Battle City tournament.

276
00:17:15,880 --> 00:17:18,292
Now everyone's going their separate ways.

277
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:21,120
I guess it's time to go. Yep.

278
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:27,100
I'm just glad that everything
turned out okay in the end.

279
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:33,100
And the winner of the Battle City
Championship crown is... Yugi Moto!

280
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,530
Yeah!

281
00:17:34,613 --> 00:17:35,940
Way to go, Yuki!

282
00:17:36,420 --> 00:17:37,917
That's what I'm going to do!

283
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:38,830
Nice duel!

284
00:17:39,220 --> 00:17:43,749
And as the winner, you get to keep the
rarest card from your opponent's deck.

285
00:17:43,840 --> 00:17:46,500
Take this, my rarest card.

286
00:17:46,780 --> 00:17:49,956
And remember, you're going
to need this card, Pharaoh.

287
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:52,240
The Winged Dragon of Ra.

288
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:56,080
We have all three of
the Egyptian God Cards.

289
00:17:56,740 --> 00:18:00,617
But now that they're in our deck,
what are we supposed to do with them?

290
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:04,818
How can we use these cards to unlock
the hidden powers of the Pharaoh?

291
00:18:05,320 --> 00:18:07,020
We need more information.

292
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:15,609
Now that Yugi has everything
he needs to finish his journey,

293
00:18:15,740 --> 00:18:17,860
I wonder if I'll ever see him again.

294
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:19,810
Hey, Taya.

295
00:18:21,040 --> 00:18:22,340
Uh, Taya?

296
00:18:24,220 --> 00:18:25,880
What? Thank you.

297
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:29,437
I know you went out of your way
to show me around the city today.

298
00:18:29,520 --> 00:18:32,480
You didn't have to, and
it meant so much to me.

299
00:18:34,800 --> 00:18:35,630
Hold on.

300
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,277
Is it two o 'clock already?

301
00:18:37,360 --> 00:18:38,700
I'm totally late.

302
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,030
Oh, no.

303
00:18:46,113 --> 00:18:48,627
Did you have something
important to do, Taya?

304
00:18:48,760 --> 00:18:49,880
Well, sort of.

305
00:18:50,440 --> 00:18:51,270
I'm sorry.

306
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:54,677
I mean, I didn't realize I was
going to mess up your plans.

307
00:18:54,760 --> 00:18:56,380
I wish you had told me.

308
00:18:56,660 --> 00:18:59,189
I never would have
dragged you around town.

309
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:00,877
Don't worry, Serenity.

310
00:19:00,960 --> 00:19:02,260
I'm not that late.

311
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:04,160
But I have to hurry.

312
00:19:04,580 --> 00:19:06,933
Before long, Yugi might be gone forever.

313
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:10,560
I mean, who knows where
fate's gonna take him next?

314
00:19:11,800 --> 00:19:12,720
Oh, well.

315
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:14,540
I have a train to catch.

316
00:19:14,900 --> 00:19:15,840
Oh, right.

317
00:19:16,140 --> 00:19:18,960
I can't believe you're
gonna be so far away.

318
00:19:19,280 --> 00:19:20,700
I won't. Huh?

319
00:19:20,940 --> 00:19:23,300
I'll be close, Teya. It's true.

320
00:19:23,640 --> 00:19:25,660
It's like Joey always tells me.

321
00:19:25,900 --> 00:19:30,724
He's connected to you guys with a special
bond of friendship that can never break.

322
00:19:30,840 --> 00:19:32,240
Joey said that to you?

323
00:19:34,580 --> 00:19:36,480
I knew he was a big softy.

324
00:19:37,060 --> 00:19:39,531
Now I feel like I'm one of you guys, Taya.

325
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:43,817
But you've always been one of us,
Serenity, ever since we first met you.

326
00:19:43,900 --> 00:19:46,140
That means we'll never be far apart.

327
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:47,460
That's right.

328
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:50,080
Bye, Taya.

329
00:19:50,540 --> 00:19:51,440
For now.

330
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:53,626
I'll see you later, Serenity.

331
00:19:56,500 --> 00:19:57,360
She's right.

332
00:19:57,640 --> 00:20:02,900
No matter how far apart I am from my friends,
they're always right here in my heart.

333
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:14,700
I know Yugi and I will always be
friends, no matter what happens next.

334
00:20:16,940 --> 00:20:19,440
But I'm not ready for him to go away yet.

335
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:23,234
I guess all I can do is enjoy
the time we have together.

336
00:20:25,060 --> 00:20:27,280
Yoo-hoo, Yugi! Over here!

337
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:29,310
Yugi!
